                         Version 1.11 Update
         
         
         Version 1.11 is mainly a bug fix for version 1.1, but there 
         are a couple of added features to make it worth the time 
         to download. 

                                      
         Adjusting SA-7s:
                                      
         The most notable new feature is the ability to automatically 
         adjust the quantity of SA-7s in the theater and in the 
         missions. You do this in the Config submode of the Other
         screen. 
         
         A new check box has been added.  It looks a little like
         this:
                                      
                   [ ]  Adjust SA-7s-Total: [     ]
                   
         If you check the box, StratFalc will run through all the 
         enemy ground paths and all the enemy sites and make sure 
         that none of them have more than the number you place in 
         the "Total" box.
         
         For example, if you place "2" in the Total box, no single 
         enemy site will be allowed to have more than 2 SA-7 squads 
         (any SA-7s in excess of this number are magically turned 
         into newts, er, transports.) In addition, no single enemy 
         ground path will have more than 2 SA-7s. Here the extra is 
         disarmed and become simple infantry squads. When you decide 
         on a quantity for this box, bear in mind that a single SA-7 
         squad has unlimited missiles. If you put "2" here, all it 
         is specifying is you'll have a maximum of 2 Grails coming at 
         you at once; you'll probably see another 2 if you make 
         another pass or stick around too long.
         
         Only values in the range of 0 to 15 are allowed. If you want 
         to eliminate SA-7s, just put the number "0" in the Total box.

         Quantities can only be adjusted down. So if you put 2 in 
         the box, all sites will drop down to 2 SA-7s, bit if you 
         then put the number 12 in the box, nothing will happen 
         immediately. With future enemy troop movements and site 
         growth, some nodes may eventually get to a strength level of 
         12.
         
         You can override the effects of this box manually using the 
         Strat/Strength submode for sites and the Tact/Enmy Ground 
         submode for paths.

         Don't forget to hit the "Save Config" button if you want 
         your settings here to be permanent.

         
         Running a User Batch File:
         
         Version 1.1 allows you to hit <F4> to run Falcon 
         immediately.  With version 1.11, you can also hit <F6> to 
         run any program(s) you desire. You define the program in a 
         batch file which you create and save as "USER.BAT"; 
         StratFalc runs USER.BAT after it exits. This feature is 
         included because many users like to run other utility 
         programs or manipulate TSRs before loading Falcon.
                                                 
         USER.BAT must be placed in the StratFalc directory or, if 
         you hit <F6>, you'll just get an error message and StratFalc 
         will dump you to DOS. 
                                                          
         If you want to return to StratFalc after the batch file 
         finishes, place the following lines in USER.BAT as the final 
         commands:        
         
                 CD \STRAT
                 STRAT.BAT %1 %2 %3 %4 %5 %6 %7 %8 %9
         
         (Change "CD \STRAT" to point to your Strategic Falcon 
         directory if you've installed it somewhere other than 
         "\STRAT.")  
                 
         For example, the following USER.BAT would exit, run 
         FalcCalc, F3 Requisition (if you own these programs), and 
         then Falcon, before returning to StratFalc: 
                            
                 CD \FCU
                 FALCCALC.EXE
                 F3REQ.EXE           
                 CD \FALCON3
                 FALCON3.EXE
                 CD \STRAT
                 STRAT.BAT %1 %2 %3 %4 %5 %6 %7 %8 %9

                       
         Bug Fixes:

         There weren't really that many!  The big one: sometimes  
         your Sim Mode aircraft wouldn't be released after a mission. 
         That's fixed.  In the Kuriles, sometimes Falcon wouldn't 
         accept new F-16 flights created with StratFalc;  that's 
         also fixed.
         
         Also, I changed the color of the background in the plane 
         description section of the loadout screen because several 
         users stated that the lack of contrast made it hard to see 
         the words (oh, you actually wanted to *read* that stuff?). 
         
         You may notice the strengths of your brigades drift a bit.
         They can go up or down, but normally they just go down. This 
         occurs because occasionally the brigades "borrow" units from 
         your sites and vice versa. It's most evident whan you send a 
         brigade into an enemy site to capture it. The original 
         strengths of brigades and squadrons have been tweaked to 
         better match the strength of the enemy Order of Battle.
         
         Finally, the docs in version 1.1 are incorrect as far as 
         RESTRCAM.BAT's implementation. Whenever StratFalc is run, it 
         checks both its own directory and the whatever directory 
         Falcon is in for RESTRCAM.BAT. If it doesn't find it, it 
         creates a new one, customized for your setup. Take a peek 
         inside RESTRCAM.BAT and you'll see what I mean.
        
         That's it.  Hope you enjoy the new features!
         
